0..72 Comment "// Law 3 of the single-substitution calculus, `sub(sub(b, p), lift(s)) ="
73..139 Comment "// sub(sub(b, s), p)`: weakening then a lifted substitution is the"
140..212 Comment "// substitution then weakening. It does not hold by computation — at a"
213..288 Comment "// variable `b` the substitution is stuck — and is proved by induction on"
289..361 Comment "// `b`, `substSquare`, from the agreement of the two composites at every"
362..427 Comment "// index: a lookup under the lift is the weakened lookup, and the"
428..473 Comment "// substitution shifting by one is weakening."
475..551 Comment "// The naturals; the syntax; the weakened lookup, the composites\' square and"
552..585 Comment "// the substitution that renames."
